. New telemetry-heartbeat PrivateTmp entries are expected consequences of the preserved service restriction, not abandoned residue.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","cmd-d178c7260fb042d5"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied: the service was repaired, runs the unchanged installed program as the existing identity, refreshes the heartbeat within five seconds, and retains its security restrictions.","limitations":["Refresh cadence was directly tested over one three-second interval rather than an extended monitoring period."]}
